[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5016416118","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121554#issuecomment-5016416118","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121554","id":5016416118,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKwBvdg","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-19T16:07:55Z","updated_at":"2026-07-19T16:07:55Z","body":"Not a bug, `Packed*Array` do not support negative indices for `remove_at` (it might be something to add to the documentation but it doesn't say it supports it so it should be assumed)\n\nIt also prints a pretty clear error:\n> Index p_index = -1 is out of bounds (prev_size = 0).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5016416118/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5016438250","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121554#issuecomment-5016438250","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121554","id":5016438250,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKwDF6g","user":{"login":"Shaderd00d","id":9315812,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzMTU4MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9315812?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shaderd00d","html_url":"https://github.com/Shaderd00d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shaderd00d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shaderd00d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shaderd00d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shaderd00d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shaderd00d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shaderd00d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shaderd00d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shaderd00d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shaderd00d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-19T16:14:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-19T16:48:35Z","body":"Update: It's best to ignore this message; it refers to a different function.\n\nI think you can tell from \"new_size\" in the method declaration that an absolute value must be specified.\n\n`int resize(new_size: int)`\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5016438250/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5016476672","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121554#issuecomment-5016476672","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121554","id":5016476672,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKwFcAA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-19T16:25:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-19T16:25:51Z","body":"This isn't about the argument of `resize` but `remove_at`\n\nIt supports negative indices for `Array` only (where it makes it clear that it is supported)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5016476672/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5037931440","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121554#issuecomment-5037931440","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121554","id":5037931440,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLEi7sA","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-21T18:59:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T18:59:06Z","body":"> Not a bug, Packed*Array do not support negative indices for remove_at\n\nWhy not implement negative indices support for packed arrays in each of their method? Or just override the `operator[]` implementations? Should these strictly only work just like their C++ counterparts?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5037931440/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5038369903","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121554#issuecomment-5038369903","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121554","id":5038369903,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLE9sbw","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-21T19:48:22Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T19:48:47Z","body":"Because that would be a pretty major change as it would require a bunch of methods be changed as well to have proper parity, it also comes with a lot of potential side effects to consider\n\nBut this should really be a [proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals) and this should focus on the changes to improve the documentation if we think any further details are needed\n\nI think the fact that it doesn't say that it supports negative indices should be enough to make it clear it doesn't, the only reason someone would think it supports it is assuming it does without no reason to. It also becomes pretty obvious with the error message from it, so I don't think a \"this doesn't work the way you might assume it does\" note in the documentation is justified. Anyone who makes this incorrect assumption will be made aware of that error by seeing the error printed","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5038369903/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5053157867","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121554#issuecomment-5053157867","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121554","id":5053157867,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLTER6w","user":{"login":"Synzorasize","id":60207816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjA3ODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60207816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize","html_url":"https://github.com/Synzorasize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T00:55:21Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T00:55:21Z","body":"> I think the fact that it doesn't say that it supports negative indices should be enough to make it clear it doesn't, the only reason someone would think it supports it is assuming it does without no reason to.\n\nIf someone sees that `Array`s support negative indices, though, they may be inclined to think that `Packed*Array`s do, too, even though the docs say that they're not supposed to be the same, but since they behave in many of the same ways, the assumption would be natural here, too.\n\nBut the workaround is just to do `array.size() - 1` or whatever negative index you want in place of `1`, therefore it's not a pressing issue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5053157867/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5055737554","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121554#issuecomment-5055737554","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121554","id":5055737554,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLVhu0g","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T07:37:35Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T07:37:35Z","body":"Supporting negative indices would involve some potentially fragile changes depending on where we make them and how it might translate to godot-cpp etc., so a bit of a complex issue to discuss in a dedicated proposal\n\nBut adding an explicit note to the docs would suffice I'd say ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5055737554/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]